### 1. Create a user (POST) -> expect 201 Created, JSON without password
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "secret123",
  "fullName": "Alice Wang",
  "age": 25
}

### 2. Get all users (GET) -> expect 200, list containing alice
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users

### 3. Get user by id (GET) -> expect 200, alice
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/1

### 4. Search users (GET) -> expect 200, alice matched by keyword
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/search?keyword=ali

### 5. Update user (PUT) -> expect 200, updated alice
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "newpass123",
  "fullName": "Alice Updated",
  "age": 26
}

### 6. Delete user (DELETE) -> expect 204 No Content
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/users/1

### 7. Get a non-existing user -> expect 404 (verifies exception layer)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/999

### 8. Duplicate username -> expect 409 Conflict (re-create alice first, then run this)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "email": "another@example.com",
  "password": "secret123",
  "fullName": "Fake Alice",
  "age": 30
}

### 9. Validation failure: blank username + bad email + weak password + negative age -> expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "123",
  "fullName": "Bad Input",
  "age": -5
}
